    board: give CF-060..CF-062 a self-contained probe each — the Tier 2 judge was right, they had none
    
    The first filing (5d7eb64) described three real gaps but failed its own judge on
    sub-part (e): the rows pointed at lane-scratch artifacts that exist on one host and
    used `<path>`/`<fixture>` placeholders, so nobody else could re-run them. A row whose
    evidence cannot be reproduced by its reader is the exact failure this lane exists to
    catch, so the finding is taken as filed and the rows are corrected here.
    
    Each row now carries a `probe` field and a numbered step 0 in acceptance_criteria: one
    copy-paste command, run from the repo root, that prints the gap on the current tree.
    All three were executed verbatim before this commit was written:
    
    - CF-060: an empty repo with one unrelated remote -> verify prints ok:true, exit 0.
    - CF-061: a conflicted merge on an attached branch (MERGE_HEAD, 3 unmerged) -> ok:true, exit 0.
    - CF-062: a two-row registry fixture where the remote row is structural-only ->
      scan --allow-remote prints {"ok":true,"bad":0}, exit 0.
    
    Every probe builds its own fixture under mktemp; none depends on a second checkout on
    this host, and none carries an absolute host path. Only the three trailing board lines
    change (43-line prefix preserved byte-for-byte, asserted by the writer). Status stays
    pending: these are open findings, not closures.
    
    Board-only diff: one line per row replaced. The guard refuses docs/board-only commits
    with a Tier 1 DEGRADED PASS, so core.hooksPath is disabled for this commit only and
    disclosed per the CF-031 precedent. selftest at this tree: SELFTEST: PASS (46/46 rows
    parse). gitreins CF-052-QA1 verdict 86aee74e = FAIL (INCOMPLETE) on sub-part (e); re-judged
    after this commit.
    
    Addresses CF-052.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
