-{"id":"CF-061","title":"P4 — lane_target.py verify passes on a checkout stuck mid-merge: MERGE_HEAD plus 3 unmerged paths still reports ok=true, the CF-049 barrier class","status":"pending","priority":"P4","complexity":2,"reasoning":"Measured 2026-11-03 by the code-factory-readme-qa lane at tip 9880018, in a throwaway clone: created a conflicted `git merge` on branch main (`.git/MERGE_HEAD` present, `git ls-files -u` = 3 entries, `git status --porcelain` first line `UU README.md`, HEAD attached to main) and `python3 -B scripts/lane_target.py verify <path>` printed ok:true and exited 0 with all six checks ok. A conflicted REBASE is caught only by accident - HEAD is detached during it, so `attached_branch` fails - which means the current protection is the detachment, not the operation. This is the same class as CF-049 (the 2026-10-30 rebase that blocked every lane for four days): nothing in the target model can see that a workdir is mid-operation, so the verifier would have blessed the blocked checkout. Probe artifact: lane-scratch qa-cf052-tip-12F1/p2.json.","acceptance_criteria":"1. verify on a local target with an in-progress operation (`.git/rebase-merge`, `.git/rebase-apply`, `MERGE_HEAD`, `CHERRY_PICK_HEAD`, `BISECT_LOG`) reports a failing check naming the marker and exits 4; the fixture must produce the state on an ATTACHED branch (a conflicted merge), because a conflicted rebase also trips the detached-HEAD check and would mask the gap.\n2. Unmerged index entries (`git ls-files -u` non-empty) also fail, with the entry count in the check's value.\n3. Negative control: a clean checkout and a clean linked worktree on a branch still exit 0.\n4. `python3 -B tests/test_lane_target.py` prints OK and `bash tests/selftest.sh` prints SELFTEST: PASS with the new fixture.\n5. specs/NODE.md's verify bullet lists the operation-marker refusal in the same commit.","created_at":"2026-11-03T12:48:52Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T12:48:52Z"}
